      "role": "user",
      "content": "That's a really good start. The tone is perfect—very \"luxury.\"\n\nBut I just checked the score on the client's tool, and it's actually pretty low. They're saying if the score isn't significantly higher, the page won't even show up in the search results for those terms. \n\nI know I said not to keyword-stuff, but we're in a bit of a bind here. Can you try a second version? Try to get that keyword count up quite a bit. Look, I still need it to be readable and high-end, but we absolutely need a much higher score to satisfy their SEO requirements. Can you do a version that's more... \"keyword-heavy\" but still tries to stay classy?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
